{"id":101,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"The tissue on the surface of its body is curiously similar in composition to an Apricorn. When irritated, this Pokémon lets loose an electric current equal to 20 lightning bolts."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Stores electrical energy inside its body. Even the slightest shock could trigger a huge explosion."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"One of Electrode’s characteristics is its attraction to electricity. It is a problematical Pokémon that congregates mostly at electrical power plants to feed on electricity that has just been generated."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Electrode eats electricity in the atmosphere. On days when lightning strikes, you can see this Pokémon exploding all over the place from eating too much electricity."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"It stores an overflowing amount of electric energy inside its body. Even a small shock makes it explode."},{"games":["X","FireRed"],"text":"It explodes in response to even minor stimuli. It is feared, with the nickname of “The Bomb Ball.”"},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It is known to drift on winds if it is bloated to bursting with stored electricity."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It is dangerous. If it has too much electricity and has nothing to do, it amuses itself by exploding."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"It stores electric energy under very high pressure. It often explodes with little or no provocation."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"They appear in great numbers at electric power plants. Because they feed on electricity, they cause massive and chaotic blackouts in nearby cities."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"The more energy it charges up, the faster it gets. But this also makes it more likely to explode."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Soundproof","hidden":false,"description":"Soundproofing gives the Pokémon full immunity to all sound-based moves."},{"name":"Static","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon is charged with static electricity and may paralyze attackers that make direct contact with it."},{"name":"Aftermath","hidden":true,"description":"Damages the attacker if it knocks out the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact."}],"eggGroups":["Mineral"],"genderRate":-1,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"urban","color":"Red","shape":"Ball","evolution":{"id":100,"name":"Voltorb","condition":null,"children":[{"id":101,"name":"Electrode","condition":"Lv. 30 or Use Leaf Stone","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,33],[1,84],[1,268],[1,598],[1,602],[9,209],[11,205],[13,103],[16,451],[20,129],[22,486],[26,120],[29,113],[36,393],[41,435],[47,153],[54,360],[58,243]],"machine":[97,268,451,174,38,598,604,486,527,203,263,492,416,360,270,63,113,319,182,240,156,184,214,164,916,129,36,269,851,168,87,86,85,521,528],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv9-48","name":"Iono's Electrode","set":"Journey Together","date":"2025-03-28","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"48","artist":null,"img":"sv9/48"},{"id":"sv4pt5-134","name":"Electrode","set":"Paldean Fates","date":"2024-01-26","rarity":"Shiny Rare","number":"134","artist":"Masakazu Fukuda","img":"sv4pt5/134"},{"id":"sv3pt5-101","name":"Electrode","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Rare","number":"101","artist":"nagimiso","img":"sv3pt5/101"},{"id":"sv2-67","name":"Electrode","set":"Paldea Evolved","date":"2023-06-09","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"67","artist":"Scav","img":"sv2/67"},{"id":"swsh11-172","name":"Hisuian Electrode V","set":"Lost Origin","date":"2022-09-09","rarity":"Rare Ultra","number":"172","artist":"5ban Graphics","img":"swsh11/172"},{"id":"swsh10-3","name":"Hisuian Electrode","set":"Astral Radiance","date":"2022-05-27","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"3","artist":"Akira Komayama","img":"swsh10/3"},{"id":"swsh8-88","name":"Electrode","s